1727e-06],[21.256113297503607,1.0202186658537324e-06],[21.936692347840815,8.444414358568641e-07],[22.636442639032587,6.994349611148034e-07],[23.34577855065165,5.812276050501746e-07],[24.07428570312528,4.833658244815217e-07],[24.817171286239837,4.027937596046192e-07],[25.574435299995322,3.363257231359387e-07],[27.136891429642713,2.3563284121663692e-07],[28.75686128185381,1.663977723189983e-07]]}],"marks":[],"legend":[["line","K","$K$, the Kretschmann scalar"],["line","R","$R^\\mu{}_\\mu$, the Ricci scalar"]],"caption":["The Kretschmann scalar $K$ and the Ricci scalar $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ of the polytropic star against $r$ ($\\kappa = 100$, central $\\rho_0 = 1.28\\times10^{-3}$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$. At the centre $K = 0.00254$ is finite, and it falls through the surface $r = R = 9.59$ into the vacuum, where $K = 48M^2/r^6$. The density and pressure fall to zero at the surface, and $K$ is continuous there.","At the centre $R^\\mu{}_\\mu = 0.0239$. Inside the star $R^\\mu{}_\\mu = 8\\pi(\\rho - 3p)$ is positive and falls outward to zero at the surface. It vanishes throughout the vacuum exterior. The star has no horizon: $g^{rr} = 1 - 2m/r$ is positive from its centre outward."],"ricci_sentences":[[1,0],[1,1],[1,2]],"per_scalar":{"kretschmann":{"opening":"The Kretschmann scalar $K$ of the polytropic star against $r$ ($\\kappa = 100$, central $\\rho_0 = 1.28\\times10^{-3}$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$.","clip":"We draw $K$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-8}$ to $10^{-2}$, and every value drawn lies within it.","legend":[["line","K","$K$, the Kretschmann scalar"]]},"ricci_scalar":{"opening":"The Ricci scalar $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ of the polytropic star against $r$ ($\\kappa = 100$, central $\\rho_0 = 1.28\\times10^{-3}$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$.","clip":"We draw $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ on a signed logarithmic scale, linear within $10^{-5}$ of zero, from $-10^{-4}$ to $10^{-1}$, and every value drawn lies within it.","legend":[["line","R","$R^\\mu{}_\\mu$, the Ricci scalar"]]}},"settings":"$G = c = M_\\odot = 1$, so lengths are in $GM_\\odot/c^2$, $K$ in its inverse fourth power and $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ in its inverse square; $M = 1.40$ and the surface radius $R = 9.59$, both rounded.","input":"A polytrope, $p = \\kappa\\rho_0^2$ and $\\rho = \\rho_0 + p$, with rest mass density $\\rho_0$, energy density $\\rho$, $\\kappa = 100$ and central $\\rho_0 = 1.28\\times10^{-3}$.","clip":"We draw $K$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-8}$ to $10^{-2}$, and every value drawn lies within it. We draw $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ on a signed logarithmic scale, linear within $10^{-5}$ of zero, from $-10^{-4}$ to $10^{-1}$, and every value drawn lies within it."}]}
